## Why This Is Asked
Tests edge routing with simple feature flag logic using standard nginx capabilities, keeping it beginner-friendly while still requiring practical setup.

## Key Concepts
- nginx upstreams and map for header-driven routing
- TLS termination in docker-compose
- cross-DC networking and service naming

## Code Example
```nginx
http {
  upstream api-old { server api-old:8080; }
  upstream api-new { server api-new:8080; }
  map $http_x_feature_flag_alpha $target { default api-old; 1 api-new; }
  server {
    listen 443 ssl;
    ssl_certificate /certs/server.crt; ssl_certificate_key /certs/server.key;
    location / { proxy_pass http://$target; }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test header-driven routing in CI?
- How would you add health checks and a safe rollback?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design tenant-aware data residency and policy enforcement in docker-dca, including edge TLS termination, overlay data paths, and canary safety net.

## Key Concepts
- docker-dca multi-DC deployment
- SPIFFE/SVID rotation with Vault
- data residency via overlay networks/volumes
- per-tenant policy with OPA
- canary rollout and rollback criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code illustrating policy check
const tenant = req.headers['x-tenant'];
if (allowedTenants[tenant]?.includes(req.path)) {
  next();
} else {
  res.status(403).send('forbidden');
}
```

